Subject: [PATCH 0013] Prism: isolate DevTools-synthetic bare Meta from macOS

BrowserNativeWidgetMac::HandleKeyboardEvent redispatches renderer-unhandled
key events into [NSApp sendEvent:] (via CommandDispatcher), which leaks them
to the macOS shortcut layer when the window is key — a bare synthetic Cmd
(MetalLeft keyDown/keyUp via Input.dispatchKeyEvent) reaches the OS there and
can launch system responses (observed: System Information).

Swallow the event when BOTH hold: it is DevTools-synthetic
(kFromDebugger — real user input never carries it) AND modifier-only
(dom_code is MetaLeft/MetaRight, i.e. no key of its own). Synthetic Cmd
chords (Cmd+C etc.) carry their own key's dom_code and redispatch exactly as
before; in-page delivery of the bare Meta is unchanged (the renderer already
saw it).
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_native_widget_mac.mm b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_native_widget_mac.mm
index 46037e7584..0a438b8298 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_native_widget_mac.mm
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_native_widget_mac.mm
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@
 #include "ui/base/l10n/l10n_util.h"
 #include "ui/base/mojom/window_show_state.mojom.h"
 #include "ui/base/ui_base_features.h"
+#include "ui/events/keycodes/dom/dom_code.h"
 #include "ui/native_theme/native_theme.h"
 #import "ui/views/cocoa/native_widget_mac_ns_window_host.h"
 #include "ui/views/interaction/element_tracker_views.h"
@@ -693,6 +694,19 @@ - (NSTouchBar*)makeTouchBar {
 
 bool BrowserNativeWidgetMac::HandleKeyboardEvent(
     const input::NativeWebKeyboardEvent& event) {
+  // Prism: swallow DevTools-synthetic *bare* Meta presses before they are
+  // redispatched into [NSApp sendEvent:] (which leaks them to the macOS
+  // shortcut layer when the window is key — bare Cmd there can trigger OS
+  // responses such as launching System Information). Only the kFromDebugger
+  // (Input.dispatchKeyEvent) traffic is affected; real user keys never carry
+  // that flag. Synthetic Cmd chords are unaffected: the chord's keyDown
+  // carries its own dom_code (e.g. KEY_C) — only a press whose dom_code IS
+  // MetaLeft/MetaRight (modifier-only, no key of its own) is swallowed.
+  if ((event.GetModifiers() & blink::WebInputEvent::kFromDebugger) &&
+      (event.dom_code == static_cast<int>(ui::DomCode::META_LEFT) ||
+       event.dom_code == static_cast<int>(ui::DomCode::META_RIGHT))) {
+    return true;
+  }
   if (!ShouldHandleKeyboardEvent(event)) {
     return false;
   }
